.\" Process this file with
.\" groff -man -Tascii timer_settime.2
.\"
.TH TIMER_SETTIME 2 "2026-07-01" "Substrate Kernel" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
timer_settime, timer_gettime \- arm/disarm and fetch a POSIX per-process timer
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library (libc, -lc)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <time.h>
.PP
.BI "int timer_settime(timer_t " timerid ", int " flags ,
.BI "                  const struct itimerspec *" new_value ,
.BI "                  struct itimerspec *" old_value ");"
.br
.BI "int timer_gettime(timer_t " timerid ", struct itimerspec *" curr_value ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR timer_settime ()
arms or disarms the timer
.IR timerid .
.PP
The
.I new_value
argument points to a
.B struct itimerspec
with two fields:
.TP
.I it_value
The time until the next expiration.  If both of its members are zero the
timer is disarmed.
.TP
.I it_interval
The reload value.  If non-zero, the timer is periodic and re-arms with this
interval after each expiration; if zero, the timer fires once.
.PP
By default
.I it_value
is interpreted relative to the timer's clock at the moment of the call.  If
.B TIMER_ABSTIME
is set in
.IR flags ,
.I it_value
is an absolute time on the timer's clock; an absolute value already in the
past causes the timer to expire as soon as possible.
.PP
If
.I old_value
is not NULL, the previous
.I it_value
(time that had been remaining) and
.I it_interval
are stored there, exactly as
.BR timer_gettime ()
would report them immediately before the call.
.PP
.BR timer_gettime ()
stores in
.I *curr_value
the time until the next expiration
.RI ( it_value )
and the reload interval
.RI ( it_interval ).
If the timer is disarmed,
.I it_value
is zero.  The reported
.I it_value
counts down; for an absolute timer it is still returned as a relative
remaining time.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, 0 is returned.  On error, \-1 is returned and
.I errno
is set to indicate the error.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I timerid
is not a valid timer, or (for
.BR timer_settime ())
a
.I new_value
field has a
.I tv_nsec
value outside [0, 999999999] or a negative
.IR tv_sec .
.TP
.B EFAULT
.IR new_value ,
.IR old_value ,
or
.I curr_value
points outside the accessible address space.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR timer_create (2),
.BR timer_delete (2),
.BR timer_getoverrun (2),
.BR clock_gettime (2),
.BR clock_getres (3)
.SH STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2008.
.SH NOTES
A
.BR timer_settime ()
call resets the timer's overrun accounting (see
.BR timer_getoverrun (2))
and discards any not-yet-accepted expiration signal for the timer.
